[size=2]Also see: [b][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/articles/12506]Intermediate: Fonts and Icons[/url][/b] (dropping or shipping files, no scripting).[/size]

[size=3]This page is for mod authors who need icon paths in [font=Courier New]RegisterGear[/font] / [font=Courier New]RegisterGizmo[/font] / [font=Courier New]Notify[/font], or who import icons at runtime with [font=Courier New]ImportIcon[/font].[/size]

[size=3]Quick map:[/size]
[list]
[*][size=3][b]Shipped layout[/b] → [font=Courier New]PrismaUI/views/COG/assets/icons/[/font] and [font=Courier New].../assets/fonts/[/font].[/size][/*]
[*][size=3][b]Runtime icon imports[/b] → [font=Courier New].../assets/imports/icons/[/font] (via [font=Courier New]ImportIcon[/font]).[/size][/*]
[/list]
[size=3]Icon imports stay in their own tree so MO2's virtual file system does not get confused when plugins write files after the game has already started. There is no font-import API yet — ship fonts under [font=Courier New]assets/fonts/[/font].[/size]

[center][img width=250]https://i.ibb.co/qL0ZKvB1/Dragonborn-Knotwork-Left.png[/img] [size=6]Shipping Icons With Your Mod[/size] [img width=250]https://i.ibb.co/gL2J92Hx/Dragonborn-Knotwork-Right.png[/img][/center]

[color=#bf9000][size=5]assets/icons + RegisterGear[/size][/color]

Put icons at the same paths your players will see under [font=Courier New]Data[/font] after install. Example:

[code]
PrismaUI/
views/
COG/
assets/
icons/
MyMod/
stress.svg
calm.svg[/code]

When you [font=Courier New]RegisterGear[/font] a gear, pass the path relative to the icons root:

[code]
COG_API.BeginRegister("MyMod", "MyMod.esp")
Int receipt = COG_API.RegisterGear("MyMod", "Stress", "percent", "Stress", "My Mod", "MyMod/stress.svg")
COG_API.EndRegister("MyMod")[/code]

No import call is needed for files that already live under [font=Courier New]assets/icons/[/font]. The editor rescans that tree when the catalog refreshes.

[center][img width=250]https://i.ibb.co/qL0ZKvB1/Dragonborn-Knotwork-Left.png[/img] [size=6]Runtime Icon Imports[/size] [img width=250]https://i.ibb.co/gL2J92Hx/Dragonborn-Knotwork-Right.png[/img][/center]

[color=#bf9000][size=5]ImportIcon[/size][/color]

When the file lives [b]outside[/b] COG's asset trees (for example under [font=Courier New]Interface/exported/...[/font] or [font=Courier New]Textures/...[/font]), call [font=Courier New]ImportIcon[/font]. COG copies or converts it into [font=Courier New]assets/imports/icons/[/font], indexes it, and returns the imports-relative path in one step:

[font=Courier New]String Function ImportIcon(String sourceMod, String iconName, String sourcePath) Global Native[/font]

[font=Courier New]sourcePath[/font] is [b]Data-relative[/b] (no absolute paths, and no [font=Courier New]Data/[/font] prefix) — for example [font=Courier New]"Interface/exported/MyMod/icon.dds"[/font]. Supported copy-as-is: [font=Courier New].svg[/font] [font=Courier New].png[/font] [font=Courier New].gif[/font] [font=Courier New].webp[/font] [font=Courier New].jpg[/font] / [font=Courier New].jpeg[/font]. [font=Courier New].dds[/font] and many other formats are converted to PNG. Returns [font=Courier New]""[/font] on failure (missing file, path escape, decode error).

The optional Example API addon ships its icon outside COG on purpose, then imports it on load. If import fails it falls back to a shipped cog so gears still register:

[code]
String Property SourceIconPath = "Interface/exported/COG_Example/example.svg" AutoReadOnly

Function COGRegisterExamples()
If !COG_API.IsReady()
Return
EndIf

String iconPath = COG_API.ImportIcon("COG_Example", "example", SourceIconPath)
If iconPath == ""
iconPath = "COG/cog.svg"
EndIf

COG_API.BeginRegister("COG_Example", "COG - Example.esp")
COG_API.RegisterGear("COG_Example", "count", "count", "Example Count", "Example", iconPath)
COG_API.EndRegister("COG_Example")
EndFunction[/code]

The optional iWant Integration does the same for real export files: it remaps known Widgets library stems to shipped COG SVGs, otherwise resolves [font=Courier New]Interface/exported/...[/font] and calls [font=Courier New]COG_API.ImportIcon[/font].

You can also hand an imported icon path to Feed toasts:

[code]
COG_API.Notify("Something happened", "#E8D2A0", "MyMod/runtime.png")[/code]

That only paints an icon when a play-visible Feed has [color=#b45f06]Notifications[/color] (and [color=#b45f06]Show icons[/color]) enabled. More toast detail: [b][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/articles/12531]Mod Author: Feed Notifications[/url][/b].

[color=#bf9000][size=5]Using Icons in Gear Registration[/size][/color]

Whether the file came from [font=Courier New]assets/icons/[/font] or from [font=Courier New]ImportIcon[/font], [font=Courier New]RegisterGear[/font] (and [font=Courier New]RegisterGizmo[/font]'s gallery icon) takes the same kind of relative path:

[code]
; Relative to assets/icons/ OR imports-relative path returned by ImportIcon
Int r = COG_API.RegisterGear("MyMod", "Focus", "percent", "Focus", "My Mod", "MyMod/focus.svg", "#DF2020", "#20DF20", "#C4A35A")[/code]

Backslashes are fine; COG normalizes them to forward slashes. If you omit the extension, [font=Courier New].svg[/font] is assumed. Pass [font=Courier New]""[/font] when the gear has no default icon.

[center][img width=250]https://i.ibb.co/qL0ZKvB1/Dragonborn-Knotwork-Left.png[/img] [size=6]Fonts[/size] [img width=250]https://i.ibb.co/gL2J92Hx/Dragonborn-Knotwork-Right.png[/img][/center]

[color=#bf9000][size=5]No Font Import API (Yet)[/size][/color]

There is no Papyrus font-import call today. Ship or drop [font=Courier New].ttf[/font] / [font=Courier New].otf[/font] / [font=Courier New].woff[/font] / [font=Courier New].woff2[/font] directly in [font=Courier New]assets/fonts/[/font] (not nested in subfolders). [font=Courier New]assets/imports/fonts/[/font] exists only for parity with icons, and may be used later if there is demand — it is far less important than icon imports. Players pick the family under [color=#b45f06]General[/color] → [color=#b45f06]Default gadget font[/color]. The Shout Meter always uses Dragon Script for the Dovahzul carving.

[center][img width=250]https://i.ibb.co/qL0ZKvB1/Dragonborn-Knotwork-Left.png[/img] [size=6]Quick Reference[/size] [img width=250]https://i.ibb.co/gL2J92Hx/Dragonborn-Knotwork-Right.png[/img][/center]
[color=#bf9000][size=5]Which Path Should I Use?[/size][/color]

[list]
[*][b]Icon ships with the mod, known at install time[/b] → [font=Courier New]assets/icons/SectionName/...[/font]. No import API.[/*]
[*][b]Icon lives outside COG assets[/b] → [font=Courier New]COG_API.ImportIcon(sourceMod, iconName, "Interface/exported/...")[/font]. Source stays put; COG writes under [font=Courier New]assets/imports/icons/[/font].[/*]
[*][b]Font ships with the mod or is a user drop[/b] → [font=Courier New]assets/fonts/[/font]. Pick it in the editor. No API call.[/*]
[/list]

[color=#bf9000][size=5]Common Pitfalls[/size][/color]

[list]
[*]Passing a path with a [font=Courier New]Data/[/font] prefix or an absolute disk path to [font=Courier New]ImportIcon[/font]: use a Data-relative path such as [font=Courier New]"Interface/exported/MyMod/icon.dds"[/font].[/*]
[*]Putting runtime writes into [font=Courier New]assets/icons/[/font] instead of [font=Courier New]assets/imports/icons/[/font]: that's how you fight MO2's VFS and lose. [font=Courier New]ImportIcon[/font] always targets the imports tree.[/*]
[*]Forgetting that the first folder is the picker section. A flat [font=Courier New]assets/icons/myicon.svg[/font] works, but a section folder keeps the picker tidy.[/*]
[*]Expecting the Shout Meter to honour the gadget font: it will not. Dragon Script stays.[/*]
[/list]

When in doubt, look at the optional [b]COG - Example API[/b] files in the installer: they ship an icon under [font=Courier New]Interface/exported/[/font], call [font=Courier New]ImportIcon[/font], and wire the returned path into [font=Courier New]RegisterGear[/font], [font=Courier New]RegisterGizmo[/font], and [font=Courier New]Notify[/font]. Copy that pattern, swap the names, and you are in business.
